  "result": "`quote` now takes a `--json` flag. With it, the command prints `{\"total_cents\": N}`; without it, the output is the same as before. All 8 tests pass when run with `python3 -m unittest discover`.\n\n**What changed:**\n- **`shop/cli.py`:** added the `--json` option to the `quote` command. It works out the total once, then prints either `json.dumps({\"total_cents\": total})` or `fmt(total)` as before.\n- **`tests/test_cli.py`** (new, since the CLI had no tests yet): two tests using `quote a:10.00:2`.\n  - `test_json_output` expects `{\"total_cents\": 2165}`.\n  - `test_default_output_unchanged` expects `21.65`.\n\n`total_cents` includes tax, because it uses the same total as the formatted output. That's why 2 \u00d7 10.00 comes out as 2165, not 2000.\n\npytest isn't installed here, so I ran the tests with `unittest`, which is the style the existing tests already use.",
